    "q-26475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q26475",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the solution to the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $6.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ \\frac{a}{3}-\\frac{b}{6}=-\\frac{5}{3} & |\\,\\times 6\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}2a+3b=-2 \\\\ 2a-b=-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $b$ in the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-b & =-10 \\\\ b & =2a+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $b=2a+10$ into the first equation and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3b & =-2 \\\\ 2a+3(2a+10) & =-2 \\\\ 2a+6a+30 & =-2 \\\\ 8a & =-32 \\\\ a & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $b,$ we substitute $a=-4$ into the equation $b=2a+10$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =2a+10 \\\\  & =2(-4)+10 \\\\  & =-8+10 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $a=-4,\\,b=2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
