    "q-208827": {
      "dom_id": "step-q208827",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the system of equations given above.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "To get rid of the fractions in the second equation, we must multiply the second equation by the lowest common denominator of the fractions, which is $3.$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{3}+4y=-\\frac{8}{3} & |\\,\\times 3\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y=7 \\\\ 2x+12y=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will use the substitution method to solve the system. Let's solve for $x$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5y & =7 \\\\ x & =5y+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we can substitute $x=5y+7$ into the second equation and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+12y & =-8 \\\\ 2(5y+7)+12y & =-8 \\\\ 10y+14+12y & =-8 \\\\ 22y+14 & =-8 \\\\ 22y & =-22 \\\\ y & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of $x,$ we substitute $y=-1$ into the equation $x=5y+7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5y+7 \\\\  & =5(-1)+7 \\\\  & =-5+7 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=2,\\,y=-1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
